              "text": "Jane and Luke have a combined age of 60.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Given that Jane is twice as old as Luke, find the ages of Luke and Jane.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Luke: 20 years; Jane: 40 years.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be Luke’s age in years. Jane’s age is $2x$ years.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+2x&=60\\\\3x&=60\\\\x&=20\\end{align*}$$\nLuke is 20 years old and Jane is $2(20)=40$ years old.\nCheck: $20+40=60$ and $40=2(20)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
